  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given, $\\begin{aligned} y & =\\tan ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-x}{1+x^{\\frac{3}{2}}}\\right) \\\\ y & =\\tan ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-x}{1+\\sqrt{x} \\cdot x}\\right) \\\\ y & =\\tan ^{-1}(\\sqrt{x})-\\tan ^{-1} x \\\\ & {\\left[\\because \\tan ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{x-y}{1+x y}\\right)=\\tan ^{-1} x-\\tan ^{-1} y\\right] }\\end{aligned}$\nDifferentiating w.r.t $x$\n$y^{\\prime}(x)=\\frac{d y}{d x}=\\frac{1}{1+x} \\times \\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{1}{1+x^2}$\nNow, $\\quad y^{\\prime}(1)=\\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}=-\\frac{1}{4}$",
    "image": null
  },
